      "text": "Given that the force \\( F \\) needed to loosen a bolt varies inversely with the length \\( L \\) of the handle of the wrench used, we can express this relationship mathematically as:\n\\[\nF \\propto \\frac{1}{L}\n\\]\nThis can be written as:\n\\[\nF = \\frac{k}{L}\n\\]\nwhere \\( k \\) is a constant. To find \\( k \\), we use the given values:\n\\[\nF = 375 \\text{ pounds} \\quad \\text{and} \\quad L = 9 \\text{ inches}\n\\]\nSubstituting these values into the equation, we get:\n\\[\n375 = \\frac{k}{9}\n\\]\nSolving for \\( k \\), we multiply both sides by 9:\n\\[\nk = 375 \\times 9 = 3375\n\\]\nNow that we have the constant \\( k \\), we can use it to find the force required for a wrench with a length of 15 inches. We substitute \\( L = 15 \\) and \\( k = 3375 \\) into the equation:\n\\[\nF = \\frac{3375}{15}\n\\]\nPerforming the division, we get:\n\\[\nF = 225\n\\]\nThus, the force required to loosen the bolt with a 15-inch handle is \\boxed{225} pounds.",
